# Stray gcloud SDK fragment accidentally created in repo root; never track or stow
google-cloud-sdk/

# Claude Code runtime.
# backups/ holds verbatim ~/.claude.json copies, MCP request headers included.
# Five carried a live CONTEXT7_API_KEY and stayed reachable from origin/main
# until the 28.07.2026 history purge. Treat it as credential material.
.claude/backups/
.claude/cache/
.claude/debug/
.claude/file-history/
.claude/history.jsonl
.claude/ide/
.claude/paste-cache/
.claude/plans/
.claude/mcp-needs-auth-cache.json
.claude/plugins/blocklist.json
.claude/plugins/cache/
.claude/plugins/install-counts-cache.json
.claude/plugins/plugin-catalog-cache.json
.claude/plugins/known_marketplaces.json
.claude/plugins/marketplaces/
# Holds machine-specific absolute install paths (differs per machine/username)
.claude/plugins/installed_plugins.json
.claude/projects/
.claude/shell-snapshots/
.claude/stats-cache.json
.claude/statsig/
.claude/tasks/
.claude/telemetry/
.claude/todos/
.claude/transcripts/
.claude/usage-data/
.claude/image-cache/
.claude/sessions/
.claude/skills/*/scripts/__pycache__/
.claude/.last-cleanup
.claude/.last-update-result.json
# Atomic-write temp files (e.g. .last-update-result.json.tmp.<hash>)
.claude/*.tmp.*
# Daemon runtime state (control.key is sensitive) and job state
.claude/daemon/
.claude/daemon.log
.claude/jobs/

# Windsurf runtime (track User/settings.json only)
Library/Application Support/Windsurf/*
!Library/Application Support/Windsurf/User/
Library/Application Support/Windsurf/User/*
!Library/Application Support/Windsurf/User/settings.json

# rtk. Track only config.toml, which is the file `rtk config` actually reads.
# The rest is runtime: history.db is 8.6 MB and grows, tee/ holds captured
# command output, filters.toml is regenerated.
Library/Application Support/rtk/*
!Library/Application Support/rtk/config.toml

# MLflow
.config/mlflow/

# Copilot runtime
.config/.copilot/

# Cagent runtime
.config/cagent/

# uv package manager
.config/uv/uv-receipt.json

# Podman Desktop
Library/LaunchAgents/io.podman_desktop.PodmanDesktop.plist

# Podman machine runtime state (generated per-machine, not authored config)
.config/containers/podman/
.config/containers/podman-connections.json
.config/containers/podman-connections.json.lock

# App-generated LaunchAgents (not authored config; apps recreate these)
Library/LaunchAgents/com.dropbox.*
Library/LaunchAgents/com.valvesoftware.*

# Editor/tool backup files (git history is the backup)
# Covers dotted-suffix variants too (e.g. *.bak.pre-copilot, *.bak.2026-04-03)
*.bak
*.bak.*

# Fonts are installed via Homebrew cask (font-fira-code-nerd-font), not vendored
fonts/

# Raycast extensions are machine-local runtime, restored per-machine by Raycast
# Cloud Sync (account-tied) — NOT by git. Vendoring them here is worse than
# useless: the compiled *.js/*.js.map/package.json are gitignored anyway, so a
# fresh checkout only ever restores icon-only `assets/` folders, which Raycast
# then reports as "Could not find command's executable JS file". Ignore the whole
# tree so git is never a source of half-populated extensions. `doctor.sh` checks
# for extensions missing their compiled JS as the safety net.
.config/raycast/extensions/
# Raycast account access token — was committed to this PUBLIC repo (rotate it in
# Raycast: sign out & back in). Untracked so it can't be re-committed.
.config/raycast/config.json

# Google Cloud SDK credentials and runtime
.config/gcloud/

# Google Workspace CLI credentials
.config/gws/

# 1Password CLI (device ID is sensitive)
.config/op/

# ngrok (contains auth token). The authtoken was committed and reachable from
# origin/main until the 28.07.2026 history purge; the whole dir is denied now.
.config/ngrok/

# Sanity CLI. config.json holds a live `authToken` that authenticates as the
# account against every project it can reach. It was tracked and public from
# 388b81b (13.05.2025) until the 28.07.2026 purge. Never track this again;
# `sanity login` recreates it locally.
.config/sanity/

# spotify-tui (client_id + client_secret). Also purged 28.07.2026.
.config/spotify-tui/

# gh CLI. hosts.yml has no token today because the macOS keyring holds it, but
# it is the exact file `gh` falls back to writing `oauth_token:` into when the
# keyring is unavailable. Default-deny, then allow the authored prefs back.
.config/gh/*
!.config/gh/config.yml

# Context7 CLI (contains API credentials)
.config/context7/

# Notion CLI (ntn) runtime
.config/notion/

# hh-observe (contains Grafana session cookies for prod/test)
.config/hh-observe/

# npm `configstore` runtime state: telemetry opt-out flags and update-check
# timestamps that the owning CLI rewrites on its own schedule (lighthouse,
# @google/gemini-cli). Nothing here is authored config. gemini-cli.json had
# already leaked in and was carrying a stale lastUpdateCheck epoch; doctor.sh's
# cruft regex only matches .bak/.mdb/*-cache.json, so these names slip past it.
.config/configstore/

# Claude plugin sweep timestamp (machine churn)
.claude/plugins/.last_inuse_sweep

# Claude Code runtime session/team state
.claude/teams/

# Installed (non-dotfiles-authored) skill symlink
.claude/skills/playwriter

# `skills add` mirrors every install into each detected agent dir. The Devin
# copies are derived output, regenerated by scripts/skills/packages.sh install,
# so they are not tracked.
#
# slack-messaging and slack-search used to be allowlisted here, described as
# "bespoke Devin skills ... authored". They were neither: both were symlinks
# into ~/.agents/skills/ pointing at targets that do not exist, committed
# broken, and they had been dangling in every fresh clone. Removed 28.07.2026
# along with ten more of the same shape under .pi/agent/skills/.
.config/devin/skills/

# Pi prompt-suggester per-project session/log state (machine churn)
.pi/agent/prompt-suggester/

# Homebrew runtime state (cask trust cache and its lock)
.config/homebrew/

# Codex. `~/.codex` is a real directory holding mostly runtime state (sessions,
# sqlite logs, plugin caches, shell snapshots). Default-deny, then allow only the
# hand-authored files that are worth stowing. Two must never be tracked:
#   auth.json   OAuth tokens
#   config.toml live API keys (GEMINI_API_KEY, X-Goog-Api-Key) plus machine churn
#               from marketplace timestamps and per-project trust levels
.codex/*
!.codex/AGENTS.md
!.codex/hooks.json
